	(text "Encoder protection: 1 k in series with each encoder signal, between the connector and the ESP32.\nStray motor or battery voltage on an encoder pin is limited to a few mA instead of killing the ESP32."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 165.1 129.54 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "090d1c09-378e-4f5f-b976-5b4255f2bda9")
	)
	(text "Motor connectors J3-J6 (JST ZH 1.5 mm, 6-pin), CHIHAI CHF-GM12-N20 pin order:\n1 = M1 (motor)   2 = encoder GND   3 = C1 (encoder A)   4 = C2 (encoder B)   5 = encoder VCC (+3V3_EXT)   6 = M2 (motor)\nOther N20 motors use other pin orders, and a wrong order can swap encoder VCC and GND. Check the cable before first power.\nEncoder outputs are 3.3 V (sensor supplied from 3.3 V); enable the ESP32 internal pull-ups for open-collector encoders."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 157.48 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "4cd12641-e996-4b2c-9488-3aa6127ce09d")
	)
	(text "Motor drivers (U8, U9: DRV8833, 2 H-bridges each) run straight from VSYS (4x AA: 4.0-6.4 V, use 6 V N20 motors).\nPer motor: IN1 = PWM, IN2 = 0 -> forward; IN1 = 0, IN2 = PWM -> reverse; both 1 = brake; both 0 = coast.\nMOT_EN high wakes both drivers; nSLEEP has an internal pull-down, so the motors stay off while the ESP32\nboots, is flashed or resets. Current limit (chopping): Itrip = 0.2 V / 0.2 ohm = 1 A per motor.\nMOT_FAULT goes low on over-current, over-temperature or under-voltage (both drivers wired-OR)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 129.54 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "c5ede141-68ad-4859-bb44-6f72c365079d")
	)
